    "result_text": "All 23 tests pass, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `membershipNumber` as a derived, read-only response field formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where YY is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year.\n\nSince it's a pure derivation of two fields already on the owner (like the existing `displayName`/`initials` derived fields), I computed it at response-mapping time rather than persisting it \u2014 no new entity field, DB column, or pipeline step needed.\n\n**Two changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipNumber` read-only property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"membershipNumber\", expression = \"java(membershipNumber(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, plus a null-safe helper:\n   ```java\n   default String membershipNumber(Owner owner) {\n       if (owner.getCustomerCode() == null || owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) return null;\n       return owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\"\n               + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);\n   }\n   ```\n   The `%02d` handles years like 2007 \u2192 `07`, and the null guard keeps owners lacking a `customerCode`/`registrationDate` (e.g. seed data) mapping cleanly instead of throwing.\n\nThe new `Cp14Tests` passes and the full suite (23 tests) is green.",
